deploy.user
  Set up a deploy account whose SSH keys are restricted
  Applies to this host.

Why
  CI that deploys with the admin's key can do anything the admin can. A separate
  account whose keys cannot forward ports or open a terminal, and with `command`
  can run only that program, limits what a leaked CI key gives away.

Params (in the module's profile table)
  name (default "deploy")
      Login name of the deploy account; not user.admin's, and not an existing
      account vps-ready did not create.
  keys (default [])
      Required: public keys without options. The account's authorized_keys holds
      exactly these, written with `restrict` (and `command=` when set).
  command (default "")
      Absolute path of a root-owned program that the keys can only run, and that
      the account may run as root with sudo, without arguments. Empty: no forced
      command and no sudo.
  docker (default false)
      Add the account to the docker group, which is root access on this host.

Fixes these audit controls
  none
